      "## Frequently Asked Questions",
      "How much should a discovery phase cost? Some agencies include it in the overall project quote; others charge a separate discovery fee, often credited toward the build if the client proceeds. Either is reasonable — what matters is that a real discovery process happens before a firm quote is given, not whether it is itemized separately. Is it a bad sign if an agency will not give a fixed price upfront? Not necessarily — for a project with genuinely undefined requirements, an agency proposing discovery first and a fixed quote after is more honest than one quoting blind. It becomes a concern only if the agency never converges on a firm number even after discovery is complete. Should we choose the cheapest agency that meets our requirements? Price matters, but the cheapest quote for comparable scope is disproportionately likely to reflect corners being cut somewhere — testing, post-launch support, or actual senior involvement. Compare total value and risk, not just the headline number. What is the biggest mistake businesses make when choosing an agency? Not checking references or live portfolio work rigorously enough, and not clarifying post-launch ownership and support terms before signing — both are easy to verify upfront and expensive to discover the hard way after the project has started.",
